<execution_sequence>
<step id="1" name="Context Resolution">
Resolve spec context **inline** using direct git/gh commands.

Execute — resolve metadata, then spec dir, then git state:
<code bash>
# ── Branch & repo metadata ──
BRANCH_NAME=$(git branch --show-current 2>/dev/null || echo "unknown")
WORKTREE_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || pwd)
COMMIT_HASH=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo "unknown")
IS_DIRTY=$([[ -n "$(git status --porcelain 2>/dev/null)" ]] && echo "true" || echo "false")
REMOTE_URL=$(git config --get remote.origin.url 2>/dev/null || echo "")

# ── Spec directory resolution ──
# Strip type prefixes (feat/, fix/, chore/, etc.) so feat/042-auth → specs/042-auth
STRIPPED_BRANCH=$(echo "$BRANCH_NAME" | sed -E 's/^(feat|fix|chore|refactor|docs|test|style|perf)\///')
BRANCH_SLUG="${STRIPPED_BRANCH//\//-}"
PARENT_SLUG=$(echo "$STRIPPED_BRANCH" | awk -F/ '{print $1}' || echo "")
if [[ -n "$PARENT_SLUG" && -d "specs/${PARENT_SLUG}/${BRANCH_SLUG}" ]]; then
  SPEC_DIR="specs/${PARENT_SLUG}/${BRANCH_SLUG}"
elif [[ -d "specs/${BRANCH_SLUG}" ]]; then
  SPEC_DIR="specs/${BRANCH_SLUG}"
else
  SPEC_DIR="specs/000-miscellaneous"
fi
SPEC_DIR_EXISTS=$([[ -d "$SPEC_DIR" ]] && echo "true" || echo "false")
WORKTREE_DETECTED=$([[ "$WORKTREE_ROOT" != "$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir 2>/dev/null | xargs -I{} dirname {} 2>/dev/null)" ]] && echo "true" || echo "false")
WORKTREE_PATH="$WORKTREE_ROOT"
CONSTITUTION_EXISTS=$([[ -f "specs/constitution.md" ]] && echo "true" || echo "false")

# ── Epic number extraction ──
EPIC_NUM=""
if [[ -n "$PARENT_SLUG" && "$STRIPPED_BRANCH" == *"/"* ]]; then
  EPIC_NUM=$(echo "$PARENT_SLUG" | grep -oE '^[0-9]+' || echo "")
fi

# ── Project type detection ──
PROJECT_TYPE=""
[[ -f "mix.exs" ]] && PROJECT_TYPE="${PROJECT_TYPE:+${PROJECT_TYPE},}elixir"
[[ -f "package.json" ]] && PROJECT_TYPE="${PROJECT_TYPE:+${PROJECT_TYPE},}node"
[[ -f "pyproject.toml" || -f "setup.py" ]] && PROJECT_TYPE="${PROJECT_TYPE:+${PROJECT_TYPE},}python"
[[ -f "Cargo.toml" ]] && PROJECT_TYPE="${PROJECT_TYPE:+${PROJECT_TYPE},}rust"
[[ -f "go.mod" ]] && PROJECT_TYPE="${PROJECT_TYPE:+${PROJECT_TYPE},}go"
PROJECT_TYPE="${PROJECT_TYPE:-undetected}"

# ── Diff and commit history ──
BASE_BRANCH=$(git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null | sed 's@^refs/remotes/origin/@@' || echo "main")
CHANGED_FILES=$(git diff --name-only "$BASE_BRANCH"...HEAD 2>/dev/null | sort | paste -sd ',' -)
COMMIT_TITLES=$(git log --pretty=format:'%s' "$BASE_BRANCH"..HEAD 2>/dev/null | paste -sd '|' -)
DIFF_SUMMARY=$(git --no-pager diff --stat "$BASE_BRANCH"...HEAD 2>/dev/null | tail -1)
</code>

Capture:
- `{BRANCH_NAME}`
- `{SPEC_DIR}`
- `{SPEC_DIR_EXISTS}`
- `{WORKTREE_ROOT}`
- `{WORKTREE_PATH}`
- `{WORKTREE_DETECTED}`
- `{CONSTITUTION_EXISTS}`
- `{EPIC_NUM}`
- `{PROJECT_TYPE}`
- `{REMOTE_URL}`
- `{COMMIT_HASH}`
- `{IS_DIRTY}`
- `{BASE_BRANCH}`
- `{CHANGED_FILES}` (comma-separated list)
- `{COMMIT_TITLES}` (pipe-separated list)
- `{DIFF_SUMMARY}`

If detached HEAD detected (branch name "unknown" or "HEAD") → emit JSON error:
<code>json
{ "Error": "Detached_HEAD", "Action": "Abort_PR_Creation" }
</code>
</step>

<step id="2" name="Repo State Check">
Check `{IS_DIRTY}`, `{CHANGED_FILES}`, `{DIFF_SUMMARY}`, `{COMMIT_TITLES}`.
If no changed files relative to base → emit `{"Error": "No_Changes_Error"}`.
</step>

<step id="3" name="Spec Detection">
Check existence: `specs/prd.md`, `{SPEC_DIR}/spec.md`, `{SPEC_DIR}/tasks.md`.
Precedence: tasks.md → spec.md → prd.md → diff/commits.
If `{SPEC_DIR_EXISTS}` is false → `"Spec_Mode": "Diff_Driven"`.
</step>

<step id="3b" name="Issue Extraction">
If `{SPEC_DIR}/spec.md` exists, parse its `[Issue]:` value from the header block. If not "N/A" → `{ISSUE_NUMBER}`. Else empty.
</step>

<step id="4" name="Phase Determination">
Phases: `Full` (Red+Green+Refactor) or `Unspecified`.
Deterministic: tasks.md phase → commit history has Red/Green/Refactor → Unspecified.
</step>

<step id="5" name="Metadata Derivation">
PR title becomes the squash merge commit message. Follow conventional commit rules from `commit.tmpl`.

<change_type>
Standard conventional commits: feat/fix/docs/refactor/chore/test/style/perf.
Derive from: (1) issue keywords, (2) diff content analysis, (3) first commit type prefix.
Fallback: `feat` for new files, `fix` for modifications.
Store as `{CHANGE_TYPE}`.
</change_type>

<title>
Format:
- `{CHANGE_TYPE}({EPIC_NUM}-{ZERO_PADDED_ISSUE}): {DESCRIPTION}` (epic + issue)
- `{CHANGE_TYPE}({ZERO_PADDED_ISSUE}): {DESCRIPTION}` (issue only)
- `{CHANGE_TYPE}: {DESCRIPTION}` (fallback)

Description from: tasks.md phase summary → dominant commit title (strip type prefix) → fallback `"update {BRANCH_NAME}"`. Zero-pad issue to 3 digits. Zero-pad epic to 3 digits where available. Max 72 chars, lowercase after colon, no period, imperative mood.
</title>

<body_template>
```markdown
{SUMMARY}

{CHANGES}

{CLOSES}
```
Summary: 2-4 sentences, what changed and why. Changes: grouped by logical concern with file refs. Closes: `Closes #N` footer when issue exists. Omit empty sections.
</body_template>

<closes>`Closes #{ISSUE_NUMBER}` if set, else omitted entirely.</closes>

<labels>Map: feat/enhancement → "enhancement", fix → "bug", refactor → "refactor", docs → "docs", chore → "chore". Sort alphabetically.</labels>

<draft>Default `false`. Override via argument flag only.</draft>
</step>

<step id="6" name="PR Body Generation">
Populate `<body_template>`: write SUMMARY (2-4 sentences, problem-led), CHANGES (grouped by concern, file refs inline), CLOSES (omit if no issue). No empty sections.
</step>

<step id="6b" name="Save PR Body">
Write to `specs/{BRANCH_NAME}/{BRANCH_NAME}.md` or `pr_descriptions/{BRANCH_NAME}.md`. Store path as `{PERMANENT_BODY_FILE}`.
</step>

<step id="6c" name="Commit PR Body">
<code>git add "{OUTPUT_DIR}/{FILENAME}"</code>
Commit: `docs(pr-description): add PR description for {BRANCH_NAME}`
Push: `git push -u origin {BRANCH_NAME}`
</step>

<step id="7" name="PR Creation">
<code>gh pr create --title "{TITLE}" --body-file "{PERMANENT_BODY_FILE}" --base "{BASE_BRANCH}" --label "{LABELS}" --draft={DRAFT}</code>
If auth fails → `{"Error": "GH_Auth_Failed"}`.
</step>

<step id="7b" name="Local Archive Rename">
Rename body file locally to include PR number (no amend, no force push):
<code>mv "{OUTPUT_DIR}/{BRANCH_NAME}.md" "{OUTPUT_DIR}/{BRANCH_NAME}-pr-{PR_NUMBER}.md"</code>
</step>
</execution_sequence>

